# Delivery Guy — environment variables
#
# These are read ONLY by the serverless function in api/holders.js, which runs
# on Vercel. index.html / styles.css / main.js are static files served straight
# to the browser: anything written into them is public. Never put a real key in
# this repo.
#
# Set the value you actually use in Vercel:
#   Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables  (Production + Preview)
# Copy this file to .env for local work; .env is gitignored.
#
# ONE of the three is enough. They are tried in this order and the first that
# answers wins. Birdeye and Solscan return the count in a single call; Helius
# has no holder-count field, so the function pages through token accounts.

# Birdeye — https://bds.birdeye.so   (free tier; sent as the X-API-KEY header)
BIRDEYE_API_KEY=

# Solscan Pro — https://pro-api.solscan.io   (sent as the "token" header)
SOLSCAN_API_KEY=

# Helius — https://dashboard.helius.dev   (free tier)
HELIUS_API_KEY=

# Optional. The function defaults to the $DELIVERY mint, so this is only needed
# if you point it at a different token.
# TOKEN_MINT=2RbedkHKGCfJ7NyeQBGWSParreAzSeAn6D8GHqLzpump
